From: Alan Shearer
Subject: virtio_net: free device id if publish_device fails

create_id() allocates a bit in a per-generator map (max 64). The id is
only a /dev/net/virtio/N path suffix. If publish_device() fails the bit
was never returned, so repeated failed probes could exhaust the generator.

---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp
@@ -1027,6 +1027,8 @@
 
 	status = sDeviceManager->publish_device(info->node, name,
 		VIRTIO_NET_DEVICE_MODULE_NAME);
+	if (status != B_OK)
+		sDeviceManager->free_id(VIRTIO_NET_DEVICE_ID_GENERATOR, id);
 
 	return status;
 }
